</code></pre> <pre><code>const p = Payload.str("hello");
p.asStr();                                   // "hello"

const j = Payload.json({ a: [1, 2] });
j.asJson();                                  // { a: [1, 2] }

const raw = new Payload([0, 1]);
raw.asBytes();                               // Uint8Array
</code></pre> <p><code>as_str</code> and <code>as_json</code> raise <code>PayloadError</code> if the bytes are not valid UTF-8 or JSON. JSON is strict: <code>NaN</code> and <code>Infinity</code> are rejected.</p>
